    "factsheet": [
        {
            "heading": "The Streatham Hill Theatre",
            "paragraphs": [
                "The Streatham Hill Theatre is a Grade II listed, 1929 Art Deco theatre designed by W.G.R. Sprague, featuring a prominent faience facade and a large 2,800-seat capacity. Streatham’s entertainment heritage continues, even as this former theatre now serves as a church.",
                "Your feet sink slightly into the thick carpet as you move forward. The sound of the outside world fades. The soft fabric underfoot muffles every step so that even walking feels gentler slower more intentional. Light spills in through high windows and settles across the curved balcony and carved details that have watched generations come and go."
            ]
        }
    ],
